Changelog: 24-11-2026 21:28:26

Fixed. The Trash shows whenever it holds a file, however small (owner, 24-11-2026). Like every place, it was left out
under 1 MB, so a Trash of a few files could not be emptied here.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 15:46:27

Fixed. The texts name the dashboard Nexus Dashboard for PS5, its new name.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 18:33:23

Fixed. The two boxes and the Delete pill now stand side by side with the row's spacing. They were spread over the width
of the window. Homebrew's row measured all of ~/.cache/Homebrew, so it came back after every Delete. brew cleanup keeps
the folders api, bootsnap and tool-selection, and the row now leaves them out. The wiki says so. .checkout-only and
.gitignore open with their license line. tools/installer-tests/garbage.sh tests install.sh, and test_garbage.py tests
Homebrew's row.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:43:13

Added. Nexus Garbage Remover, a development app. It lists the garbage on this machine: crash dumps, Steam's crash
reports, the Trash, picture previews, pip's download cache and Homebrew's downloads, each with its size and the
command that empties it. Delete empties the checked places after it asks, the crash dumps through pkexec. An hourly
timer sends a notification from 1 GB on, once a day or sooner when it grew by 1 GB. Our tools' own leftovers stay
with tools/clean_caches.py.
